  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 227 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nRain tapers off in southeast Iowa before pushing east on Sunday\nmorning. Breezy northwest winds gusting to 20-25 mph will usher\nmuch colder air into the state with highs on Sunday in the 40s.\nBy Monday highs will range from the mid 30s in northern Iowa to\nlow 40s in southern Iowa. Highs in the 30s to low 40s will last\nthrough the upcoming week, including the Thanksgiving holiday. \nThose with travel plans will be glad to know that the forecast \nthrough next week looks to remain dry. Right now there are a \ncouple weak shortwaves next week moving across the central US, \nhowever at this time they either track away from Iowa or are dry\npassages. Details on these will be monitored for any impactful \nchanges.",
